# QEMU host isolation (dev & deploy)

**Goal:** keep the Windows host clean. All runtime (Docker, Ansible, compose, Gradle `:run` stacks, smokes against live stack) runs **inside QEMU guests**, not on the host OS.

## Allowed on the host

- Edit repo, git, Gradle **tests/build** (`buildIntegrity`, unit tests) when they do not require a live stack
- **QEMU lifecycle only:** `scripts/qemu-up.ps1`, `scripts/qemu-dev-up.ps1`, `scripts/qemu-down.ps1`, `scripts/qemu-redeploy.ps1`, `scripts/qemu-watch.ps1`, `scripts/qemu-logs.ps1`, `scripts/ensure-qemu-images.ps1`
- Browser / Playwright against **forwarded ports** (API `127.0.0.1:18080`, UI `127.0.0.1:19088`)
- Host scripts that **orchestrate VMs** (repo snapshot HTTP, cloud-init) — see `deploy/qemu/`

## Forbidden on the host (use VMs instead)

- `docker compose`, `docker build`, Docker Desktop install for dev stacks
- `ansible-playbook` against real deploy targets (except docs-only dry runs)
- `scripts/full-stack-up.ps1`, `scripts/dev-web-stack-up.ps1`, `scripts/korus-web-up.ps1`, `scripts/run-core-api-local.ps1`, `scripts/dev-infra-up.ps1`, `scripts/install-env-silent.ps1` (Docker)
- Long-running `:modules:*:run` for server/web against host-local infra

## Where runtime lives

| VM | IP (guest LAN) | Role | Host ports |
|----|----------------|------|------------|
| `korus-server` | 192.168.76.10 | Docker full-server + Ansible `qemu-server-local` | 18080, 18082, 18081 |
| `korus-web` | 192.168.76.20 | korus-web + Ansible `qemu-web-local` | 19088 |

Bootstrap/redeploy **inside guests:** `deploy/qemu/vm-bootstrap/run-ansible-local.sh` → `deploy/ansible/playbooks/qemu-*.yml`.

Docs: [`deploy/qemu/README.md`](deploy/qemu/README.md), [`deploy/ansible/README.md`](deploy/ansible/README.md).

## Agent workflow

1. Start stack: `.\scripts\qemu-up.ps1` (or `-KeepDisks` / `qemu-redeploy.ps1` for code refresh).
2. Verify: `http://127.0.0.1:18080/api/v1/health`, `http://127.0.0.1:19088/`.
3. Run smokes/ansible/docker **in the server or web guest** (SSH or documented VM paths), not on the host.
4. If QEMU is down, **start/fix QEMU first** — do not fall back to host Docker.

## Exceptions

- CI / GitHub Actions (Linux runners) — not the Windows dev host.
- Explicit user request to run something on the host despite this rule.
